<title>UK: Ghana cocoa purchases behind year earlier.</title>
<headline>Ghana cocoa purchases behind year earlier.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ghana cocoa purchases to the end of the 15th week of the 1996/97 season, ending January 23, were a cumulative 260,506 tonnes compared with 303,867 tonnes at the end of the 16th week of the year-earlier season.</p>
<p>The 16th week of the 1995/96 season ended on January 25, 1996.</p>
<p>The Ghana Cocoa Board said it purchased 15,138 tonnes of cocoa in the 15th week of 1996/97, compared with 7,803 tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>In the 15th week of the 1995/96 season, which ended on January 18, Ghana purchased 8,798 tonnes of cocoa, bringing the cumulative seasonal total to 296,064 tonnes.</p>
